//! Keel's API (spec 2.10, "API and automation"): one compile-time list of typed operations,
//! [`OPS`], serves JSON-RPC (`keel-daemon`), the `keel` CLI subcommands and the MCP server
//! (`keel mcp`). Each [`Operation`] has a name, a summary, JSON schemas for its parameters
//! and result (generated by `schemars` from the Rust types in [`types`]) and a handler.
//!
//! Mutating operations are preview-first: called directly, they only validate their input
//! and return a [`types::PlanPreview`] (a plan id plus the hash of the exact input);
//! `execute` with that id and hash applies it, refusing tampered or expired plans. File
//! operations go through `plan` (keel-core's `validate -> preview -> execute`). Only
//! `shares.revoke` (taking access away) and `recents.note` (an opened file) act directly.
//! Mounts (`mounts.*`) need a host that serves them ([`Ctx::mounts`], set by keel-daemon).

